# Bulleted work lists, added to by every branch. A union merge keeps both
# sides' lines, so concurrent additions never conflict. Its cost: an entry
# one side closes and the other edits comes back, one edited on both sides
# stays in both forms, and two wrapped additions sharing a line can splice.
# The next reader tidies those; no gate reads these files.
/TODO.md merge=union
/docs/todo-performance.md merge=union
